{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthnRequestParamsMode"},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s12CaseIterableP","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/Se","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SE","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SQ","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SH","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SY","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether this client’s authorization requests may carry OpenID Connect’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authentication-request parameters, or whether they are ignored (X7.1). The bundle this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"governs is "},{"code":"prompt","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"max_age","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"acr_values","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"claims","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"id_token_hint","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"login_hint","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"display","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"ui_locales","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"claims_locales","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one"}]},{"type":"text","text":" field rather than nine booleans"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for the same reason ["},{"code":"ClientProfile","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] is one field rather than a dozen: a client that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"honours "},{"code":"max_age","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" but ignores "},{"code":"prompt=none","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is not “mostly conformant”, it is a client a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relying party cannot reason about. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"Self::Ignore"},{"type":"text","text":" is the serde default and is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly what AXIAM has always done — unknown authorization-request parameters are dropped by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the query deserialiser and never reach a decision. Every row written before schema v54"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"therefore decodes to the behaviour it already had."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/authnrequestparamsmode"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Enumeration","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK22AuthnRequestParamsModeO","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AuthnRequestParamsMode","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"symbolKind":"enum","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AuthnRequestParamsMode","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"AuthnRequestParamsMode","role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AuthnRequestParamsMode"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"open","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" enum. A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list decodes to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than failing the response it arrived in (CONTRACT.md §27.11 rule 1). Throwing there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fails the WHOLE response, so one field of one record would take down the page it was on,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"including the records the caller did ask for."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is never read as one of the KNOWN cases: reading a new value as whichever case happens to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be first turns a new server state into a wrong one, and on this surface these values gate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own raw value is the empty string, which no server value is, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"carrying an unrecognised value back into an update is refused by the server rather than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written as a spelling it never used. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" over these cases needs an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" arm."}]}]}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthnRequestParamsMode\/honour","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthnRequestParamsMode\/ignore","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthnRequestParamsMode\/unknown"],"title":"Enumeration Cases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthnRequestParamsMode\/init(from:)-18mcn","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthnRequestParamsMode\/init(rawValue:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthnRequestParamsMode\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthnRequestParamsMode\/RawRepresentable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AuthnRequestParamsMode/unknown":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/authnrequestparamsmode\/unkn